WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.310
Film Courage: Now that you’ve explained
the 6-stages and we’ve already talked about

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:08.270
Stage 1 (the set-up) can you also talk about
what happens in Stage 2 (we’re still in

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.270
Act 1).

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.690
Michael Hauge: Yes.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:16.789
So I said at the 10 percent point of the story
something that has never happened to the hero

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:19.939
before is going to happen and that is the
Opportunity.

00:00:19.939 --> 00:00:25.160
It can be something good, meeting the person
of their dreams if it’s a romantic comedy,

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.160
let’s say.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:31.620
It can be something terrible, like the first
body of the horror movie is discovered or

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:36.220
the spaceship that the aliens are landing
on earth in shows up.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:41.330
Whether it’s good or bad, it’s going to
be something that forces the hero into Stage

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.690
2 into a new situation.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:48.610
And in this stage the primary goal of the
character is to figure out what’s going

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:50.860
on (I’ve entered this new world).

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.660
Sometimes in movies it’s even a change in
geography.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:58.780
To go back to quite an old movie now, THELMA
AND LOUISE, it’s when they leave town and

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:04.500
go out to spend the weekend at some guy’s
cabin or something like that.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:11.780
In THE FIRM, when he takes the job with Bendini,
Lambert &amp; Locke and he and his wife head to

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:12.780
Memphis.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.440
It could be a geographical change, it might
not be.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:20.310
But they are in a new situation and they have
to figure out “What am I doing here?

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.380
What are the rules of this world I have entered.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:27.140
What is expected of me or how do I deal with
the news of the discovery of that body?

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:34.070
Or what am I going to do with this person
I just met?”

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:39.120
A movie that I really enjoyed a lot this year
is EYE IN THE SKY.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:45.281
And we meet our hero Helen Mirren waking up
and we see her living her every day life and

00:01:45.281 --> 00:01:49.659
we see that she is in the military and so
on and when she gets a call and when she gets

00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:57.740
to the base or wherever it is, she discovers
that they have found or they have confirmed

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:04.540
that a group of bad guys, particularly these
two Americans have shown up and she’s been

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:05.540
doggin’ after them.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:11.009
So she’s got to figure out how are we going
to be following them or capturing them once

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:12.009
they are all together.

00:02:12.009 --> 00:02:14.430
She’s trying to figure out “What do I
do?”

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:22.350
On the inner journey level in Stage 1 we see
the character living fully in his identity.

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:26.080
Okay, like I mentioned Will Hunting in GOOD
WILL HUNTING.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.260
Or if you take a character like Hitch (HITCH
Movie) who has also had his heart broken,

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:31.400
so he is shut down.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:35.860
He will help other people find love but he
doesn’t believe in love for himself.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.440
He’s stuck.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.810
Stage 2, the character is still in his identity.

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:47.420
Still fully protected but the character will
get a glimpse of what living fully, what living

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.020
in his essence might be like.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:57.101
So that is in HITCH when he first meets Albert
Brenneman, the Kevin James character, for

00:02:57.101 --> 00:03:04.250
all of his schlubby personality is way more
courageous and way more understanding of the

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.000
value of falling in love than Hitch is.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.340
So he gets just a look at what that might
be like.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:14.620
He doesn’t really register but we recognize
“Okay, this is what this person needs to

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:15.620
learn.”

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:21.080
We recognize early on in this story this is
the journey this character needs to go on

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.410
inside.

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:30.030
And then at the end of Stage 2 comes what
I call the Change of Plans, another key turning

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.030
point.

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:36.560
Another thing happens that has never happened
before and that is going to move the character

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:42.890
from figuring out what is going on to formulating
the goal, the visible goal and taking the

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:45.790
first steps to achieve it.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:49.959
So, when that happens, let’s go back to
EYE IN THE SKY.

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:57.120
What happens there is they discover that these
bad guys have moved to a different location.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:03.830
The location they can’t go in to capture
the bad guys because it will create chaos

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:04.830
outside.

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:10.280
The only way they can stop them is to use
a drone, send something at them, and take

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.280
them out.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.590
Obliterate them, just send them into oblivion.

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:23.449
So now the outer motivation for Helen Mirren
becomes she wants to use a dart or a drone

00:04:23.449 --> 00:04:26.080
to take out the bad guys in this building.

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:31.710
And the rest of the movie will be her pursuit
of the goal and all the obstacles she will

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:35.860
encounter in trying to get there, all of the
conflict.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:40.409
And I didn’t mention it but I should have
mentioned this earlier in the interview, but

00:04:40.409 --> 00:04:44.430
I’ll say it now…I began this by saying
the primary goal of any storyteller is to

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:46.259
illicit emotion.

00:04:46.259 --> 00:04:52.270
One thing that is critical to understand is
emotion comes out of conflict, not desire.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:57.520
So the more you can build up the obstacles
your characters have to face, the more emotionally

00:04:57.520 --> 00:07:17.009
involved the story will be.

